## 1. Project Mission & Identity
TrueGaze™ is an official gaming and virtual world product derived from Kirk LaSalle's Human Communication Eye Protocol (HCEP). Its mission is to eradicate the "dead-eye syndrome" and robotic neck movements in game engines, beginning with The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim (SE, AE, and VR) and expanding to modern game engines.

TrueGaze models true biological human oculomotor dynamics:
1. Saccades via the empirical Main Sequence equation (peak velocity 700-900 deg/s, duration 20-50ms).
2. Vestibulo-Ocular Reflex (VOR): Eyes lead target acquisition in 20-30ms; head/neck follow with higher inertia (120-180ms); eyes counter-rotate to preserve foveal lock.
3. Micro-Saccadic Brownian Drift (1-3 Hz physiological jitter) preventing frozen stare.
4. Cognitive Gaze Aversion (Glenberg et al., 1998) mapping to HCEP THINK mode.
5. Social Triangle Scanpaths (Argyle & Cook, 1976) mapping to HCEP AFFECT mode.
6. Saccadic Eyelid Blinks coupled with Expressive Facegen Morphs (EFM).
7. Deep Open Animation Replacer (OAR) integration: Exposes custom native C++ conditions so modders can trigger custom body animations and gestures when NPCs enter HCEP modes or achieve mutual gaze.

